{"repositoryId":697026114,"availability":"available","full":"alperencelik/kubemox","name":"kubemox","description":"Proxmox operator for Kubernetes to manage Proxmox resources.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":99,"forks":11,"created":"2023-09-26T22:46:49Z","updated":"2026-10-14T13:04:58Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://alperencelik.github.io/kubemox","topics":["kubernetes","kubernetes-operator","operator","proxmox","proxmox-ve"],"demo":"https://alperencelik.github.io/kubemox","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T05:28:19.923Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T05:28:19.923Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T05:28:19.923Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T05:00:52.566Z","stars":99,"forks":11},{"at":"2026-10-20T05:28:19.923Z","stars":99,"forks":11}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Kubemox is a Proxmox operator for Kubernetes. It allows you to create and manage Proxmox VMs from Kubernetes.","Proxmox is a great open-source virtualization platform. It has a great API and CLI but managing resources inside Proxmox within a declarative way might be hard. Kubemox is a Kubernetes operator that allows you to manage Proxmox resources in a declarative way. It brings the power of Kubernetes to Proxmox and allows you to manage Proxmox resources with Kubernetes resources with the endless control loop of Kubernetes."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alperencelik/kubemox/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d57c2704a21bb63668fdafa8028bd06a3a9ac33d3683e5f529fcf595964f4b7f","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T05:00:52.910Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T05:00:52.910Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Kubemox is a Proxmox operator for Kubernetes. It allows you to create and manage Proxmox VMs from Kubernetes.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alperencelik/kubemox/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d57c2704a21bb63668fdafa8028b